=== (1) FREE ALGEBRA, CHECKED BEFORE THE RUN — uniform attenuation cannot flatten a row ===
  observed  bracket A (`abpoorw`) +0.6449 · **bracket B (`abdefctw`) -0.0239**  n=1960
  row scaled by 1.0 (classical attenuation): B = -0.0239
  row scaled by 0.7 (classical attenuation): B = -0.0239
  row scaled by 0.4 (classical attenuation): B = -0.0239
  row scaled by 0.2 (classical attenuation): B = -0.0239
  ⇒ **B is invariant to ANY per-row scalar.** So 'the medical item is a worse MEASURE' in the
     classical attenuation sense is ALREADY refuted — algebra, labelled as a DERIVATION, not
     evidence. World ITEM survives only as 'the item loads on a different MIX', a content
     claim. ⚠ this narrows register-item ⑥ of `#892`; it does not settle it.

