=== (8) WHY THE PRE-REGISTRATION MISSED, AND WHAT THE GRID ACTUALLY SHOWS ===
  ⚠ **The kill predicted the WRONG SIGN, and it inherited that from `#892`.** The card said
     ABS ⇒ `B > 0` among differentiators, because `#892` had read B ≈ 0 as *flat*. Once the
     baseline is right, `B* < 0` everywhere — **the medical norm couples PREFERENTIALLY to
     medical legality items**, which is case-specificity, not its absence. A pre-registration
     built on a mis-priced quantity cannot be rescued by re-reading it after the fact, so the
     verdict on the PRE-REGISTERED question stays `UNVERIFIED` (`#111c`: one, not two).

